TICKET = "Issue: reset: restart auto-adjusted miniters\n\n## Description\n\n`tqdm.reset()` preserves the auto-adjusted `miniters` from the previous run when `miniters=None` (the default with `smoothing`), so a reused bar whose early phase had large steps can freeze: the threshold stays at hundreds while the new phase updates one item at a time, and the display never refreshes.\n\nReset now clears `miniters` when `dynamic_miniters` is active, restarting auto-adjustment for the new run, matching the way `reset()` already rebuilds the EMA state. Explicit `miniters=` values are kept.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom tqdm import tqdm\nimport time\nt = tqdm(total=1000, smoothing=0.3)  # default miniters=None\nfor _ in range(200):  # first run: large steps raise dynamic miniters\n    time.sleep(0.01); t.update()\nt.reset(total=100)\nfor i in range(100):  # second run: 1-item steps never hit the old threshold\n    time.sleep(0.01); t.update()\nt.close()\n```\n\nThe second pass barely redraws. After the fix it refreshes normally.\n\n### Validation\n\n- New regression `test_reset_dynamic_miniters` fails on `master` and passes with the fix.\n- Full suite: 168 passed, 12 skipped.\n\nI plan to open an accompanying issue with this reproduction if that's the preferred flow.\n\nPrepared with AI assistance (a coding agent audited the reset path, reproduced and fixed the defect); submitted by the account owner.\n"

